      "title": "Career & Alumni Support",
      "description": "Career & Alumni Support | Morningside University Skip to main menu Skip to content Career & Alumni Support St. Luke’s College to join Morningside University. Read the full press release and FAQs Admissions Start Your Experience At Morningside, you don't just apply for a degree, you embark on a journey to shape your identity, broaden your perspectives, and prepare for a successful future. Admissions Home Undergraduate Students Undergraduate Admissions Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Graduate Students Graduate Admissions Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Cost & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Why Morningside? Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Contact Admissions Academics Shape Your Future With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Academics Home Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Explore more than 65+ majors and pre-professional programs Graduate Programs Post-Bachelor's degrees and certificates Bachelor's Completion Programs Non-traditional student Bachelor degrees High School Student Programs Programs for current high school students Academic Opportunities Internships & Externships Study Abroad & May Term Schools & Departments Academic Schools School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academic Resources Academic Calendars Library Academic Support Career & Alumni Support Research Information Technology Academic Catalogs Registrar Athletics Student Life + Arts Live and Learn With a commitment to lifelong learning, Morningside is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Student Life + Arts Home Life at Morningside Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Get Involved Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Arts at Morningside Performing Arts Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Visual Arts Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Visit Apply Give Search Morningside Undergraduate programs | Graduate programs Faculty/staff directory | Contact us Morningside University / Academics / Career & Alumni Support Career & Alumni Support Apply Schedule Visit CAREER SERVICES LET US HELP YOU BUILD NEW CONNECTIONS At Morningside University, our Career Services are tailored to make your professional aspirations a reality, no matter where you are on your career path. Whether you’re a current student seeking internship opportunities, a senior planning your initial career trajectory, or an alum looking for a fresh start in a new field, we’re here to support you every step of the way. UNLOCK YOUR CAREER POTENTIAL WITH HANDSHAKE Morningside University Career Services uses Handshake to communicate employment opportunities to students, new graduates, and alumni. Handshake can help you discover new career paths, find amazing jobs & internships, and connect with great companies & non-profits. The site is protected, so to get access, you must register. Administrators at Morningside will then approve your request. Find Your Next Career If you are having trouble registering please contact Stacie Hays . Get Involved HELP STUDENTS & ALUMS FIND OPPORTUNITIES Do you have an open internship or job opening? Use Handshake to post the opening to Morningside students and alumni! Follow the instructions above to create your Handshake account, then post your opportunity. Handshake SHARE YOUR EXPERTISE If you have expertise in a particular area and might be interested in serving as a guest speaker for a class or workshop, let us know! Fill out this form , or contact Alex Watters or Stacie Hays in Career Services for more information. Fill out this Form VISITING CAMPUS OR GUEST SPEAKING FOR A CLASS? Whether you are helping out as a guest speaker or just visiting campus for fun, please let us know you were here so we can send you a little token of our appreciation for staying in touch. Check in Form Questions? Stacie Hays Associate Vice President of Career Services & Professional Development Krone Advising Center 712-274-5032 hays@morningside.edu Main Menu Information For Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts Visit Apply Give About Morningside Mside Store News Events Employment Sitemap Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Overview Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Why Morningside? Why Morningside? Overview Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Admissions Admissions Overview Undergraduate Admissions Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Contact Admissions Why Morningside? Academic Schools Academic Schools Overview School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing