is a hub for rigorous academic inquiry and scholarly excellence providing students the knowledge they need to succeed. Student Life + Arts Home Life at Morningside Living on Campus Eating on Campus Campus Services Campus Ministry Campus Safety & Security Disability Services Information Technology Student Health & Wellness Athletic & Fitness Facilities Get Involved Volunteering & Engagement Siouxland Community Leadership Development Arts at Morningside Performing Arts Choral Music Instrumental Music Theatre Camps, Festivals, Workshops Christmas at Morningside CODA Legacy Awards Visual Arts Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Visit Apply Give Search Morningside Undergraduate programs | Graduate programs Faculty/staff directory | Contact us Morningside University / About Morningside / Employment Morningside Employment WORK AT MORNINGSIDE JOIN OUR TEAM Located in Sioux City, IA, Morningside is a great place to launch or continue your career. Our campus is a welcoming and warm place, and like our students, faculty, and staff generally find that their community of colleagues also quickly become friends. View our job openings below . Download Application 2023 GREAT COLLEGE TO WORK FOR®” Morningside University is one of the best colleges in the nation to work for according to the Great Colleges to Work For® program. Learn More RESOURCES How to Apply Simply download our PDF application and email the following to employment@morningside.edu : The completed application Your cover letter and resume Anything else specified within the job description Be sure to specify which of our open positions you’re applying for. Handbooks Faculty Handbook Staff Handbooks Siouxland Community New to the area? The Siouxland community is a perfect example of city meets small town, a wonderful place to call home. Our beautiful parks, great schools, low cost of living, and access to numerous retailers and resources are just a few of the perks of living here. Living in Siouxland Contact HR Department If you have any questions, please contact our HR department at (712) 274-5114 or send an email to employment@morningside.edu . We’re here to help. Employment Opportunities Part-Time Faculty Adjunct Instructors - Rosen School of Business Full-Time Faculty Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology Assistant Professor of History Assistant Professor of Special Education Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Business Administration Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Staff Associate Registrar Electrical Technician / HVAC Support Housekeeper HVAC & General Electrical Technician Part-Time Staff Graduate Assistant for Athletic Operations Main Menu Information For Future Students Current Students Alumni & Friends Faculty/Staff Admissions Academics Athletics Student Life + Arts Visit Apply Give About Morningside Mside Store News Events Employment Sitemap Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Visit Morningside Apply to Morningside Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Returning Students Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Overview Elementary Education (Online) RN to BSN (Online) Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Graduate Business Graduate Education Graduate Nursing Why Morningside? Why Morningside? Overview Sioux City Values & Outcomes Our Guarantee Stang Stories Admissions Admissions Overview Undergraduate Admissions Complete Your Bachelor’s Degree Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Access to Mside Siouxland Proud, Mside Bound Contact Admissions Why Morningside? Academic Schools Academic Schools Overview School of Agriculture & Aviation School of Arts & Sciences Rosen School of Business Nylen School of Nursing & Health Sciences Sharon Walker School of Education School of Visual & Performing Arts Academics Academics Overview Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Bachelor's 